<title>USA: UroMed sees Q4 loss $0.21-$0.23/shr.</title>
<headline>UroMed sees Q4 loss $0.21-$0.23/shr.</headline>
<dateline>NEEDHAM, Mass. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>UroMed Corp said Thursday it expects to report a loss of $0.21-$0.23 a share and revenues of $500,000 for the 1996 fourth quarter.</p>
<p>For the year, UroMed said it expects a loss of $1.87-$1.89 a share.</p>
<p>It said the loss includes a one-time charge of $30.2 million, or $1.18 per share, accounted for as purchased research and development, relating to the acquisition of Impress Miniguard and all incontinence technology of the Advanced Surgical Intervention Liquidating Trust.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
